{"agent_id":"anon-b19d58ac","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:27:01.852764762Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e344a032-c88e-48fd-a660-f46361a0227b","title":"Divergence: ls -v size_packed / ls -j sizes.packed print the raw header rom_size 0; upstream normalises rom_size to buffer_size (header_file.py:72-73)","description":"Upstream (PSPTool 241629b, /tmp/psptool-ref/psptool/header_file.py:72-73):\n    if self.rom_size == 0:\n        self.rom_size = self.buffer_size\nThe HeaderFile attribute rom_size is normalised to the file buffer size (the directory entry size, file.py:297-299, grown to 0x100 at header_file.py:32-33). Both listings print the normalised value: ls -v `hex(file.rom_size)` in size_packed (psptool.py:183-189) and ls -j `'packed': file.rom_size` (psptool.py:261-265).\n\nTarget: psptool-ops/src/list.rs:355 (text, `format_hex_u64(h.rom_size as u64)`) and :463 (JSON, `\"packed\": h.rom_size`) render the RAW header field HeaderEntry::rom_size (entry.rs:199), so a header with rom_size == 0 prints 0x0 / 0.\n\nRepro: psptool AORUS_X370G5.23d -E -v -> PSP_FW_BOOT_LOADER~0x1 @0x268000 size_packed 0x0 (upstream 0x8000); SMU_OFFCHIP_FW~0x8 @0x270000 0x0 (upstream 0x14000).\n\nImpact (corpus, 147 HeaderFiles): 39 0x1/0x8 entries of the Summit-Ridge combo directories (Acer_R01-A4, AORUS_X370G5, ASRock A320/B350/X370, ASUS PRIME A320/B350/X370/X470, ROG STRIX B350/X370/X470), plus 0x3/0xc/0x10/0x12/0x14 entries and 0x2e PREMIUM_CHIPSET_MP0_DXIO_FW on AORUS_X570_X57AOXT2.FCd (Zen 2/3). Note Entry::file_bytes(blob).len() already equals upstream's normalised value on the whole corpus.\n\nFailing tests: crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_headerfile_list_values.rs::divergence_size_packed_normalises_zero_rom_size, ::divergence_json_sizes_packed_normalises_zero_rom_size (synthetic) and ::divergence_corpus_sizes_packed_matches_reference (live reference, 147 mismatches). Control control_size_packed_nonzero_rom_size passes.","priority":"medium","created_by":"anon-b19d58ac"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-b19d58ac","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:27:07.266767714Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"e344a032-c88e-48fd-a660-f46361a0227b","label":"blocker"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-b19d58ac","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:27:13.422491960Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a249be78-533d-4cb8-b9e7-69f2f9dd67f6","title":"Divergence: ls MD5 of a HeaderFile hashes the whole entry; upstream HeaderFile.md5 hashes self.body = [0x100, rom_size - signature_len) (header_file.py:106,312-315)","description":"Upstream (PSPTool 241629b, /tmp/psptool-ref/psptool/header_file.py:312-315) overrides File.md5 (file.py:380-383) for HeaderFile and its KeyStoreFile subclass:\n    def md5(self):\n        m = md5()\n        try:\n            m.update(self.body.get_bytes())\nself.body is the data region NestedBuffer(self, len(self) - len(self.header) - self.signature_len, len(self.header)) (header_file.py:106), i.e. [0x100, rom_size - signature_len) - not the whole entry. ls -v prints file.md5()[:4].upper() (psptool.py:180), ls -j 'md5': file.md5()[:4].upper() (psptool.py:254).\n\nTarget: the sparse (\"upstream-exact\", #87) MD5 cell is body_md5_short_upper(&e.body) (psptool-ops/src/list.rs:346, :672-674) and the JSON md5 is body_md5_hex(&e.body) (list.rs:455): both hash the whole directory-declared entry (header + data + signature). Correct for File/PubkeyFile/MicrocodeFile, wrong for every HeaderFile-class entry. The #87 pin (divergence_list_columns.rs) only checks length/case on a non-HeaderFile (WRAPPED_IKEK), so it never saw this.\n\nRepro: PSPTOOL_LS_SPARSE=1 psptool AORUS_X370G5.23d -E -v -> PSP_FW_BOOT_LOADER @0x268000 MD5 93B4 (upstream C985 = md5(f.body.get_bytes())[:4]); SMU_OFFCHIP_FW @0x270000 F658 (upstream A83B).\n\nImpact (corpus): 4147 HeaderFile-class entries, i.e. every 0x1/0x2/0x8/0x24/0x28/0x39 (and other HeaderFile) entry of every image incl. EPYC Milan H12SSW9.719 and Zen 2/3 X570/A520M. JSON md5 presence/format (only with -v, 32-char) is #94; this issue is the hashed bytes.\n\nFailing tests: crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_headerfile_list_values.rs::divergence_sparse_md5_hashes_headerfile_body (synthetic) and ::divergence_corpus_headerfile_md5_matches_reference (live reference, 4147 mismatches).","priority":"medium","created_by":"anon-b19d58ac"}}
