{"agent_id":"anon-b19d58ac","agent_seq":16,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:39:21.590327973Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"293b1344-0dcf-4e79-b0ae-f57bd981696f","title":"Divergence: ls -v fills size_signed/size_full/size_packed/load_addr for a KeyStoreFile; upstream only for type(file) is HeaderFile (psptool.py:183-191)","description":"Upstream (PSPTool 241629b, /tmp/psptool-ref/psptool/psptool.py:183-191):\n    if type(file) is HeaderFile:\n        all_values += [hex(v) for v in [file.size_signed, file.size_uncompressed, file.rom_size, file.load_addr]]\n    else:\n        all_values += (4 * [''])\n`type(file) is HeaderFile` excludes the KeyStoreFile subclass (key_store_file.py:23; KEY_STORE_TYPES 0x50/0x51, file.py:244), so a KeyStoreFile ls -v row has empty size_signed / size_full / size_packed / load_addr. (The JSON sizes block uses issubclass, psptool.py:260, and does include KeyStoreFile.)\n\nTarget: psptool-ops/src/list.rs build_entry_row (list.rs:350-359) fills the four cells for every e.class.header(), which includes EntryClass::KeyStore (entry.rs EntryClass::header).\n\nRepro: psptool <any image with a 0x50/0x51 key store> -E -v -> BL_PUBLIC_KEY~0x50 row size_signed/size_full/size_packed/load_addr populated; upstream empty.\n\nImpact (corpus): 12 KeyStoreFile rows, 6 each in ASRock-A520M-HSV-1.31.ROM and AORUS_X570_X57AOXT2.FCd (the only corpus images with key stores).\n\nFailing tests: crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_list_text_headerfile_cells.rs::divergence_keystore_row_has_empty_size_columns (synthetic) and ::divergence_corpus_keystore_size_columns_match_reference (live reference ls -v table, 12 rows).","priority":"low","created_by":"anon-b19d58ac"}}
